; Leftover assembler source text
;
; 64 bytes of text from the source file of the program (an assembler's line
; buffer left in memory), cut off at $9C3F where the sprite data at #R$9C40
; begins. Nothing references it. Readable parts: "NZ,ENDPAUSE", "INC E",
; "JR NZ,PAUSE", "INC D", "JR NZ,PAUSE", i.e. the lines of a delay loop with
; labels PAUSE and ENDPAUSE. The lines are split into fields by TAB ($09); each
; line seems to be preceded by a 2-byte prefix ("J" $06 or "J" $0C for the
; instruction part) and followed by a byte that grows by $21 per line
; ($82, $A3, $C4, $E5, $06); the meaning of those bytes is Unknown.
@label=LeftoverSource
